        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Daina Reid, Peter Helliar, Bryan Keith Strauchan, Daniel Willis\n- Works: I Love You Too\n- Roles: director, screenwriter, comedian, actor, presenter, writer, producer, director, fictional football player, clergyman\n- Organizations: Anglican Diocese of Sydney\n- Topics: Australian film, Australian rules football\n\nFacts:\n- Daniel Willis was born on 8 April 1954 in Herberton and is an Australian clergyman who spent most of his adult life in the Anglican Diocese of Sydney.\n- Peter Helliar was born on 16 June 1975 and is an Australian-born comedian, actor, radio and television presenter, writer, producer, and director.\n- Bryan Keith Strauchan, also known as Strauchanie, is a fictional Australian rules football player portrayed by Peter Helliar who first appeared in short sketches on Before the Game.\n- I Love You Too is a 2010 Australian romantic comedy film and was the directorial film debut of Daina Reid.\n- Peter Helliar wrote the screenplay for I Love You Too as a first-time writer.",
